   "type": "text",
   "text": "**Q0** · question\n\nCan CLSS DNA tie-seam surgery strictly lower expected DNA density on >=1 (w,k) cell in OrensteinLab/10-minimizers and GreedyMini by >=0.5% relative?",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "5"
  },
  {
   "id": "H1",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**H1** · hypothesis\n\nSOS-DP Fast Zeta Transform O(w * 2^(w-1)) over tie-window submasks accelerates exact prob_gc_dna local search by >10,000x and beats binary-only GreedyMini on (w=12, k=4) by >=0.5% relative",
   "x": 420,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "6"
  },
  {
   "id": "H2",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "✗ **H2** · hypothesis\n\n4-ary de Bruijn transfer-matrix DP over 4^k states without primary-bit compression can find a compact non-binary order for (w=12, k=4)\n\n*why dead:* Unneeded: strict binary-to-DNA permutation [15,6,7,12,10,4,11,3,0,1,8,9,14,2,13,5] in identical 136-byte .gm format already achieves -1.7763% relative (3.55x the 0.5% threshold) with 100% tie-break equivalence between GreedyMini and 10-minimizers",
   "x": 420,
   "y": 220,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "1"
  },
  {
   "id": "E1",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**E1** · experiment\n\nsos_dna_optimizer.cpp (SOS-DP + SA + Steepest-Descent 2/3-Cycle Polish) across 48 precomputed .gm cells: strictly improved 17 cells by >=0.5% relative (up to -4.274% at w=8,k=3) and lowered flagship (w=12, k=4) from 0.1360458389 to 0.1336292920 (-1.7763% rel)",
   "x": 840,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "3"
  },
  {
   "id": "R1",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**R1** · result\n\nFlagship (w=12, k=4) strict permutation w12_k4_improved.gm achieves exact expected DNA density 573,933,439 / 2^32 = 0.1336292920 vs 584,312,429 / 2^32 = 0.1360458389 (-1.7763% rel); 17 precomputed (w,k) cells improved by >=0.5% rel",
   "x": 1260,
